# ROOT08 issuer worker — bounded storage adaptation and retained authority gate

Task PACC-PHASE6-ROOT08-ISSUER-WORKER-INTEGRATION-3MIB-1. main / c50b8fb9a7e3293b5e6355fc08459bf85b56857a. Prior Windows-profile manifest: all 200 hashes matched; baseline 4216 existing files. No accepted norm or historical artifact changed.

## Applied scope

Official executor approved the exact two-header capacity hunks, their global-layout correction, separation from historical synchronous scratch, and the census-only hunk; every operation checks SHA256 preimages and postimages. No executor rejection occurred. Stages/operations/patches preserve every intermediate preimage. Only these existing files changed: server_configuration_pending_win32.h, server_configuration_commit_win32.h, phase6_memory_census_test.c.

The explicit Windows 3 MiB build selector alone chooses transaction storage 28960. All translation units must share that selector. No local worker flag participates in struct layout. Default/legacy remains16896. The existing owner's committed array and the existing packet previous/next arrays use this capacity; observed remains512. The historical PAPACC_CONFIG_STORAGE_BYTES stays16896 (8192 outside C8); it continues bounding the two local arrays in the old synchronous commit. Thus enlarging committed does not silently enlarge that path's stack. Codec sizes/layouts and historical issuer constants remain unchanged.

No second buffer, allocator, root, registry, thread, queue or journal was added. Existing snapshots and pins are unchanged. Three separately owned images can coexist; none is overlaid. Immutable previous/next remain frozen before worker exposure; old committed remains intact through CAS conflict/UNKNOWN and Stop. Capacity alone never selects a format, promotes resolution, acquires authority, changes grants or publishes CURRENT.

## Exact dependent STOP

T4/T5 in DECISION-server-tls-identity-persistence-revision2-20261020 require the selected full predecessor image, actual CURRENT/base pin, matching durable checkpoint, source leases and independently preserved association/approval history. For first v1->v2 adoption they require an explicit authorized same-root transition; historical ROOT06 is not an admissible predecessor.

The actual entry papacc_configuration_d3_begin08 in server_configuration_pending_win32.inc currently validates only pc_root8_validate_no_issuer and pc_root8_base_link, rejects every issuer-bearing slot and bounds images to PC_ROOT8_NO_ISSUER_MAX. pending_d3_packet_valid in server_configuration_d3_worker_win32.inc explicitly recognizes version1 without issuer. Export repeats these restrictions. Those guards remain BYTE-EXACT. Removing them is not a storage change.

The existing v2 carrier callback is DATA ONLY: it receives a caller-borrowed floor and workspace, returns views with epoch/proofs0, verifies serialized identity/history and rejects CERT_BOUND without actual DER/SAN authority. It does not supply a CURRENT pin or a source lease/approval chain. config_root8_v2 exposes data encode/decode/validate, not a qualified full-predecessor authority transition. A decoded CP or successful hash cannot fill that gap. No approved first-adoption source/lease proof was located in these entry paths. No CURRENT was manufactured to make a positive v2 worker test possible.

Consequently v2 dispatch/commit/export attachment is NOT implemented or qualified. The dependent integration stops at this authority/lifetime boundary; existing v1/ROOT06 behavior is preserved. Storage capacity is ready, but this task is PARTIAL. This is not an executor denial, a new normative decision, or a request to reopen accepted contracts.

## Minimum continuation, same owner

Before extending begin/poll/export, connect the existing factual root/source owners: acquire actual current ticket and matching issuer generation snapshot, hold source borrow for the complete approved listener/security/TLS/name/issuer tuple, verify complete predecessor CP R/A/P/I/C/W against actual owner and native file identity, and verify the full association/issuer history. Copy complete immutable previous/next into the existing packet before releasing caller borrows. Add an explicit version2 discriminator only after this validation; unknown/malformed versions must never fall back. Keep v1/ROOT06 branches byte-exact. No v2 bootstrap or ROOT06 migration.

Compare native full predecessor bytes under the same worker transaction; preserve committed and retained packet through conflict/UNKNOWN/Stop. No private signing, operational CURRENT, fabricated epochs or automatic retries. Positive native filesystem/CAS over a synthetic administrative fixture must remain labelled synthetic CURRENT, not qualified product authority. Full TLS/X509 consumption and authoritative recovery remain separate gates.

## Accounting and validation limits

See ed11-census.json and compiled-census.json. Charge three maximum arrays separately, plus existing issuer snapshots/staging, 512-byte observation, worker stack and owner scratch. Candidate encode prefix/output costs are separate caller storage, not new permanent buffers. No retained or pinned bytes were reused and no quota/reservation reduced. Full transitive callback/native activation peak and provider/kernel resources remain UNKNOWN; ED11_TOTAL_STATUS stays PARTIAL.

Initial selected tests exposed inconsistent struct layout under a translation-unit-local selector. The official correction made selection global; incremental objects still failed, while a clean rebuild passed both codec executables. Initial logs remain. Final builds/tests are recorded separately. The new census verifies all three allocated capacities and the preserved observation size. Native regression fixtures exercise existing v1 and ROOT06 paths, not v2 commit, real CA creation, private signing, or operational publication.

Browser, PST, PACC wire, production0.6.4 and accepted documents remain unchanged. Box/ISA are not qualified. Admission, signature, CURRENT and authoritative recovery remain DENY. PST0.6.5 remains deferred until Phase6 completion.
